{
  "$schema": "https://jxsuite.com/schema/v1",
  "$id": "StudioMediaPane",
  "$description": "The Media viewer: a pane that SHOWS a file the studio has no document model for — an image at its own size, a video or audio player, an embedded PDF, a font set in a pangram, or an honest line about a format nothing here can draw. The adapter hands in one projection: which of the six stages to draw, the URL that loads it, the file's name and facts, the reference a document would write for it, and the documents that already do. Nothing here decides anything; a control asks the host to copy, to open a path, or to record the pixel size the browser just learned.",
  "tagName": "div",
  "attributes": {
    "part": "viewer",
    "data-jx-region": "${state.region}"
  },
  "style": {
    "$description": "What `.media-viewer`, `.media-stage`, `.media-image`, `.media-video`, `.media-embed`, `.media-audio`, `.media-specimen`, `.media-specimen-line`, `.media-unviewable`, `.media-note`, `.media-details`, `.media-name`, `.media-facts`, `.media-ref`, `.media-ref-value`, `.media-usage`, `.media-usage-title`, `.media-usage-headline`, `.media-usage-list`, `.media-usage-link` and `.media-usage-count` said in `styles/overlays.css`, keyed on `part` and re-pointed at the studio token layer. All twenty-two were this surface's alone, so the stylesheet block goes with the conversion rather than being copied. Eight `var(--spectrum-font-size-…)` names could not come with the declarations: every one of them resolves only inside `<sp-theme>`, and this document is mounted in a pane stage that is outside it, so each would silently have taken its hex fallback — they are the kit's `--jx-text-xs`, `--jx-text-sm`, `--jx-text-md` and `--jx-text-lg` instead.",
    "height": "100%",
    "display": "flex",
    "gap": "var(--jx-space-5)",
    "padding": "var(--jx-space-5)",
    "overflowY": "auto",
    "background": "var(--bg-panel)",
    "fontFamily": "var(--jx-font-sans)",
    "color": "var(--fg)",
    "& [part=\"asset-slot\"], & [part=\"usage-slot\"], & [part=\"list-slot\"]": {
      "$description": "A `$switch` renders its own container, and none of these three is a box: each stands exactly where its case does, so the case's own rule is the only one that lays anything out.",
      "display": "contents"
    },
    "& [part=\"stage\"]": {
      "$description": "The asset takes the room and the details column keeps a fixed width, so the file is the thing being looked at and the facts about it are beside it rather than on top of it.",
      "flex": "1",
      "minWidth": "0",
      "display": "flex",
      "alignItems": "flex-start",
      "justifyContent": "center"
    },
    "& [part=\"image\"]": {
      "$description": "Never larger than its own pixels: an upscaled thumbnail is a lie about the asset, and judging whether an imported image is big enough is the whole reason somebody opens this.",
      "maxWidth": "100%",
      "height": "auto",
      "border": "1px solid var(--border)",
      "borderRadius": "var(--radius)",
      "background": "var(--bg-input)"
    },
    "& [part=\"video\"], & [part=\"embed\"]": {
      "width": "100%",
      "maxHeight": "70vh",
      "border": "1px solid var(--border)",
      "borderRadius": "var(--radius)",
      "background": "var(--bg-input)"
    },
    "& [part=\"audio\"]": {
      "width": "100%"
    },
    "& [part=\"specimen\"]": {
      "$description": "A font is shown by being USED. The face itself arrives as a `@font-face` the adapter writes, under a family name generated from the path so two specimens open side by side cannot claim the same one; the element carries only that NAME, as a custom property, and the fallback stack that catches a face the browser refuses stays here where it is a rule rather than data.",
      "width": "100%",
      "padding": "var(--jx-space-5)",
      "border": "1px solid var(--border)",
      "borderRadius": "var(--radius)",
      "background": "var(--bg-input)",
      "color": "var(--fg)",
      "fontFamily": "var(--jx-specimen-family, system-ui), system-ui, sans-serif"
    },
    "& [part=\"specimen-line\"]": {
      "margin": "0 0 var(--jx-space-4)",
      "lineHeight": "1.3",
      "overflowWrap": "anywhere"
    },
    "& [part=\"specimen-line\"][data-size=\"48\"]": {
      "fontSize": "48px"
    },
    "& [part=\"specimen-line\"][data-size=\"32\"]": {
      "fontSize": "32px"
    },
    "& [part=\"specimen-line\"][data-size=\"24\"]": {
      "fontSize": "24px"
    },
    "& [part=\"specimen-line\"][data-size=\"18\"]": {
      "fontSize": "18px"
    },
    "& [part=\"specimen-line\"][data-size=\"14\"]": {
      "fontSize": "var(--jx-text-lg)"
    },
    "& [part=\"unviewable\"]": {
      "$description": "Not a failure state. A file the browser cannot render is a zip, or a format this build has never heard of, so the box says what the file IS and that the project still builds with it in.",
      "padding": "var(--jx-space-6)",
      "border": "1px dashed var(--border)",
      "borderRadius": "var(--radius)",
      "color": "var(--fg-dim)",
      "textAlign": "center"
    },
    "& [part=\"note\"]": {
      "fontSize": "var(--jx-text-md)",
      "color": "var(--fg-dim)"
    },
    "& [part=\"details\"]": {
      "flex": "0 0 260px",
      "display": "flex",
      "flexDirection": "column",
      "gap": "var(--jx-space-4)"
    },
    "& [part=\"title\"]": {
      "margin": "0",
      "fontSize": "var(--jx-text-lg)",
      "color": "var(--fg)",
      "overflowWrap": "anywhere"
    },
    "& [part=\"facts\"]": {
      "$description": "Kind, pixel size, bytes and modified date, joined by the adapter. Each is omitted rather than zeroed when it is not known: a real file can almost be `0 × 0` or `0 B`, so neither may double as \"we did not find out\".",
      "margin": "0",
      "fontSize": "var(--jx-text-md)",
      "color": "var(--fg-dim)"
    },
    "& [part=\"ref\"]": {
      "$description": "The reference a document writes for this file — `/hero.jpg` for `public/hero.jpg`, which shares not one segment with it. Getting this wrong is the commonest way an image goes missing from a page, which is why it is on screen next to a button that copies it.",
      "display": "flex",
      "alignItems": "center",
      "gap": "6px"
    },
    "& [part=\"ref-value\"]": {
      "flex": "1",
      "minWidth": "0",
      "fontFamily": "var(--font-mono)",
      "fontSize": "var(--jx-text-sm)",
      "background": "var(--bg-input)",
      "border": "1px solid var(--border)",
      "borderRadius": "var(--radius)",
      "padding": "3px 6px",
      "overflowWrap": "anywhere"
    },
    "& [part=\"usage\"]": {
      "display": "flex",
      "flexDirection": "column"
    },
    "& [part=\"group-title\"]": {
      "margin": "0 0 var(--jx-space-2)",
      "fontSize": "var(--jx-text-md)",
      "fontWeight": "500",
      "color": "var(--fg-dim)"
    },
    "& [part=\"message\"]": {
      "margin": "0",
      "fontSize": "var(--jx-text-md)",
      "color": "var(--fg-dim)"
    },
    "& [part=\"list\"]": {
      "listStyle": "none",
      "margin": "var(--jx-space-3) 0 0",
      "padding": "0",
      "display": "flex",
      "flexDirection": "column",
      "gap": "var(--jx-space-1)"
    },
    "& [part=\"row\"]": {
      "display": "flex",
      "alignItems": "baseline",
      "gap": "6px",
      "fontSize": "var(--jx-text-md)"
    },
    "& [part=\"file-path\"]": {
      "$description": "The path is a control, not a label: it opens the document that references this file. A plain button rather than a `jx-button`, for the reason the Problems rows give — what it has to look like is a line of text, and every fill, border and control height the kit draws would have to be taken back off again. Named `file-path` and not `path` because `jx-icon` puts `part=\"path\"` on the `<path>` of every glyph it draws, so `[part=\"path\"]` would select this button and any SVG path beside it.",
      "flex": "1",
      "minWidth": "0",
      "margin": "0",
      "padding": "0",
      "background": "none",
      "border": "none",
      "borderRadius": "var(--jx-radius-xs)",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "color": "var(--accent)",
      "cursor": "pointer",
      "font": "inherit",
      "overflowWrap": "anywhere",
      ":hover": {
        "textDecoration": "underline"
      },
      ":focus-visible": {
        "outline": "var(--jx-focus-ring)",
        "outlineOffset": "2px"
      }
    },
    "& [part=\"count\"]": {
      "flex": "0 0 auto",
      "fontFamily": "var(--font-mono)",
      "fontSize": "var(--jx-text-xs)",
      "color": "var(--fg-dim)"
    }
  },
  "children": [
    {
      "tagName": "div",
      "attributes": {
        "part": "stage"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tagName": "div",
          "attributes": {
            "part": "asset-slot",
            "role": "none"
          },
          "$switch": {
            "$ref": "#/state/kind"
          },
          "cases": {
            "image": {
              "tagName": "img",
              "attributes": {
                "part": "image",
                "src": "${state.src}",
                "alt": ""
              },
              "onload": {
                "$prototype": "Function",
                "body": [
                  {
                    "operator": "call",
                    "target": {
                      "$ref": "#/state/imageLoaded"
                    },
                    "value": [
                      {
                        "$ref": "event#/target/naturalWidth"
                      },
                      {
                        "$ref": "event#/target/naturalHeight"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "description": "The only honest source of pixel dimensions in a browser is an image that has loaded, and this viewer is showing one at full size anyway. The host decides whether the numbers are new; a repeat load of the same picture must not repaint the pane."
              }
            },
            "video": {
              "tagName": "video",
              "attributes": {
                "part": "video",
                "src": "${state.src}",
                "controls": true
              }
            },
            "audio": {
              "tagName": "audio",
              "attributes": {
                "part": "audio",
                "src": "${state.src}",
                "controls": true
              }
            },
            "embed": {
              "tagName": "embed",
              "attributes": {
                "part": "embed",
                "src": "${state.src}",
                "type": "application/pdf",
                "title": "${state.name}"
              }
            },
            "font": {
              "tagName": "div",
              "attributes": {
                "part": "specimen",
                "style": "${state.specimenFamily}"
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "tagName": "style",
                  "textContent": "${state.fontFace}"
                },
                {
                  "tagName": "p",
                  "attributes": {
                    "part": "specimen-line",
                    "data-size": "48"
                  },
                  "textContent": "${state.specimen}"
                },
                {
                  "tagName": "p",
                  "attributes": {
                    "part": "specimen-line",
                    "data-size": "32"
                  },
                  "textContent": "${state.specimen}"
                },
                {
                  "tagName": "p",
                  "attributes": {
                    "part": "specimen-line",
                    "data-size": "24"
                  },
                  "textContent": "${state.specimen}"
                },
                {
                  "tagName": "p",
                  "attributes": {
                    "part": "specimen-line",
                    "data-size": "18"
                  },
                  "textContent": "${state.specimen}"
                },
                {
                  "tagName": "p",
                  "attributes": {
                    "part": "specimen-line",
                    "data-size": "14"
                  },
                  "textContent": "${state.specimen}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "unviewable": {
              "tagName": "div",
              "attributes": {
                "part": "unviewable"
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "tagName": "p",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "tagName": "span",
                      "textContent": "Jx has no viewer for "
                    },
                    {
                      "tagName": "code",
                      "textContent": "${state.extLabel}"
                    },
                    {
                      "tagName": "span",
                      "textContent": "."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "tagName": "p",
                  "attributes": {
                    "part": "note"
                  },
                  "textContent": "The file is in the project and builds normally."
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tagName": "div",
      "attributes": {
        "part": "details"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tagName": "h3",
          "attributes": {
            "part": "title"
          },
          "textContent": "${state.name}"
        },
        {
          "tagName": "p",
          "attributes": {
            "part": "facts"
          },
          "textContent": "${state.facts}"
        },
        {
          "tagName": "div",
          "attributes": {
            "part": "ref"
          },
          "children": [
            {
              "tagName": "code",
              "attributes": {
                "part": "ref-value"
              },
              "textContent": "${state.ref}"
            },
            {
              "tagName": "jx-action-button",
              "$props": {
                "size": "sm",
                "quiet": true,
                "hint": "Copy the reference"
              },
              "attributes": {
                "part": "copy"
              },
              "onclick": {
                "$prototype": "Function",
                "body": [
                  {
                    "operator": "call",
                    "target": {
                      "$ref": "#/state/copyRef"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "tagName": "span",
                  "textContent": "Copy"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tagName": "div",
          "attributes": {
            "part": "usage-slot",
            "role": "none"
          },
          "$switch": {
            "$ref": "#/state/usageState"
          },
          "cases": {
            "shown": {
              "tagName": "div",
              "attributes": {
                "part": "usage"
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "tagName": "h4",
                  "attributes": {
                    "part": "group-title"
                  },
                  "textContent": "Used by"
                },
                {
                  "tagName": "p",
                  "attributes": {
                    "part": "message"
                  },
                  "textContent": "${state.usageHeadline}"
                },
                {
                  "tagName": "div",
                  "attributes": {
                    "part": "list-slot",
                    "role": "none"
                  },
                  "$switch": {
                    "$ref": "#/state/hasUsageFiles"
                  },
                  "cases": {
                    "true": {
                      "tagName": "ul",
                      "attributes": {
                        "part": "list"
                      },
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "$prototype": "Array",
                          "items": {
                            "$ref": "#/state/usageFiles"
                          },
                          "key": {
                            "$ref": "$map/item/path"
                          },
                          "map": {
                            "tagName": "li",
                            "attributes": {
                              "part": "row",
                              "data-usage": "${$map.item.path}"
                            },
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "tagName": "button",
                                "attributes": {
                                  "part": "file-path",
                                  "type": "button"
                                },
                                "textContent": "${$map.item.path}",
                                "onclick": {
                                  "$prototype": "Function",
                                  "body": [
                                    {
                                      "operator": "call",
                                      "target": {
                                        "$ref": "#/state/openDocument"
                                      },
                                      "value": [
                                        {
                                          "$ref": "$map/item/path"
                                        }
                                      ]
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              },
                              {
                                "tagName": "span",
                                "attributes": {
                                  "part": "count"
                                },
                                "textContent": "${$map.item.count}"
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
